### IPP-305 password recovery tests
### How to use: run `npm run dev` in /server, then click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### Put the SAME verified email you used in 304-login.http (line 7)
@email = arsalmustafa62+ipp2@gmail.com

### Requests 4, 6 and 7 need the token from the reset email (sent by request 2):
### the link looks like http://localhost:5173/reset-password/<64 characters>
### copy those 64 characters and paste after "@resetToken = ".
### (The same link is also printed in the server terminal as "[dev] Reset link ...")
@resetToken = 0b015f78d74d47d524f0145adc90780507d2ab000a7fa4aa8f403ce8ece9563a

### Login token from request 1, picked up automatically. Used in request 8.
@oldToken = {{oldLogin.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Log in with the CURRENT password and keep the token -> expect 200
###    (request 8 checks that this token stops working after the reset)
# @name oldLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 2. Forgot password -> expect 200 "If this email is registered, a password reset link has been sent..."
###    Check your inbox (and spam) for "Reset your Interview Prep Portal password".
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}


### 3. Forgot password for an email that is not registered -> expect the SAME 200 message (no email is sent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody-here@example.com"
}


### 4. Reset with a weak password -> expect 400 "Password must be 6 to 72 characters"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password/{{resetToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "1"
}


### 5. Broken link -> expect 400 "Invalid reset link"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password/abc123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "secret456"
}


### 6. Reset with the token from the email -> expect 200 "Password changed. Please log in with your new password"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password/{{resetToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "secret456"
}


### 7. Same link again -> expect 400 "This reset link is invalid or has expired..." (each link works once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password/{{resetToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "another789"
}


### 8. Old login token (from request 1) -> expect 401 "Your password was changed. Please log in again"
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{oldToken}}


### 9. Login with the OLD password -> expect 401 "Invalid email or password"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 10. Login with the NEW password -> expect 200 "Logged in successfully"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "secret456"
}


### NOTE: this account's password is now secret456.
### To run 304-login.http again, change "secret123" to "secret456" in its requests 6 (and 2 stays wrong on purpose).
